-- title:
--   Non-split twisted class: δ₀σ(δ₀) central and twisted commutant a division algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ of degree $2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (so $\sigma$ generates $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$), let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, let $c$ be a unit of $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ (with $\mathbb{A}_K$ the adele ring of $K$), and let $u$ be a unit of $\mathbb{A}_K$. Assume: (i) the twisted norm string of length $\mathrm{finrank}_K L = 2$, namely the product $\delta\cdot\sigma(\delta)$ where $\delta$ is the image of $\delta_0$ under $\ell \mapsto \ell\otimes 1$ multiplied by the scalar matrix $c$, and where $\sigma$ acts entrywise through its extension to $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ on the left factor, equals the scalar matrix with entry $1 \otimes u$; and (ii) for every $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and every $z \in L^\times$ one has $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(x) \neq z\cdot 1$, i.e. $\delta_0$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate to a scalar matrix. Then both of the following hold: there exists $z \in L^\times$ with $\delta_0\,\sigma(\delta_0) = z \cdot 1$; and every $x \in M_2(L)$ satisfying $x\delta_0 = \delta_0\,x^{\sigma}$ (entrywise application of $\sigma$) and $x \neq 0$ is invertible.
--
--   The statement descends the adelic central-norm condition on $\delta_0 c$ to the rational condition $\delta_0\sigma(\delta_0) \in L^\times\cdot 1$, and then records that the $\sigma$-twisted commutant $\{x \in M_2(L) : x\delta_0 = \delta_0 x^{\sigma}\}$ of a non-split twisted class is a division algebra; it is the twisted analogue, for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ and a quadratic extension, of the fact that the centraliser of a regular elliptic element is a field. It is used downstream in the computation of twisted orbital integrals and in the determinant and basis statements attached to the twisted commutant, and its proof cites the unique-solvability result [`AutomorphicForm.existsUnique_mul_eq_mul_map_and_mulVec_eq_of_forall_ne_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.existsUnique_mul_eq_mul_map_and_mulVec_eq_of_forall_ne_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two).
